      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## ServiceNow SLA Breach Predictor & Escalator\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow polls ServiceNow every 15 minutes for open incidents, extracts key fields, groups tickets by category, and processes them in batches. For each item it calculates an SLA breach probability, optionally fetches historical resolution data with a wait-controlled loop, and checks whether the predicted risk exceeds 70%. High-risk incidents are reassigned/escalated in ServiceNow, annotated with a work note, and announced to a manager in Slack; low-risk incidents pass through without action.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure ServiceNow credentials for all ServiceNow nodes and verify the instance URL, table, filters for open incidents, update fields for assignment escalation, and work note content.\n- Configure Slack credentials and set the manager channel or user target for the notification node.\n- Review the schedule trigger interval and enable the workflow when ready.\n- Validate the custom code in the category grouping and breach probability nodes against your incident fields and SLA policy.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the breach-risk threshold, polling interval, ticket grouping logic, escalation assignment target, Slack message text, and any batch/limit settings to match your support process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "17a35d8d-03cc-40a1-89a6-850178113471",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
